From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: log a run-once keyed wait that ends without its
 release

RtlRunOnceBeginInitialize queues a waiter by pointing the once at a
variable on the waiter's stack, and RtlRunOnceComplete walks that list,
reading each waiter's link before releasing it. If NtWaitForKeyedEvent
returns without that release, the waiter loops, may see the once done
and return, and the completer then reads a link in a dead frame. Hollow
Knight on Direct3D 12 ended 1 s in with an access violation in
RtlRunOnceComplete reading such a link (garbage: 0x1280000836002500,
then x86 code bytes), from UnityPlayer's InitOnceComplete on a static
once, in 3 of 13 starts.

Waiting again until the wait reports success hung every Direct3D 12
start (7 of 7), so the wait does end without a release here, and keeps
doing so. This logs the status (the first 16 times) and keeps Wine's
behaviour, to find out which status and why before a fix.

Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-06-vulkan-perf-baseline.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 dlls/ntdll/sync.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/sync.c b/dlls/ntdll/sync.c
index 58094e2..db1d74e 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/sync.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/sync.c
@@ -142,7 +142,18 @@ DWORD WINAPI RtlRunOnceBeginInitialize( RTL_RUN_ONCE *once, ULONG flags, void **
             next = val & ~3;
             if (InterlockedCompareExchangePointer( &once->Ptr, (void *)((ULONG_PTR)&next | 1),
                                                    (void *)val ) == (void *)val)
-                NtWaitForKeyedEvent( 0, &next, FALSE, NULL );
+            {
+                /* Playport: once queued, this frame is the completer's list node
+                 * until RtlRunOnceComplete releases it (it reads next first). Log
+                 * a wait that ends without the release: then the frame can go
+                 * while the completer may still read it. Waiting again on such a
+                 * status hung every Direct3D 12 start of Hollow Knight (the wait
+                 * kept failing at once), so the status is only logged for now. */
+                static LONG logged;
+                NTSTATUS status = NtWaitForKeyedEvent( 0, &next, FALSE, NULL );
+                if (status && InterlockedIncrement( &logged ) <= 16)
+                    ERR( "once %p: keyed wait returned %#lx without a release\n", once, (long)status );
+            }
             break;
 
         case 2:  /* done */
